# Code ownership for NeuViTech Labs.
#
# Every pull request already requires a review from the other track. These
# rules add a required owner on the paths where a mistake is expensive or
# hard to reverse. With two engineers, an owner entry names both, because
# GitHub does not count a pull request's own author toward its required
# review, so listing both means the other person is always the required
# reviewer without anyone having to decide who owns what each time.
#
# As the team grows, these entries become the real ownership map, with
# different owners per area. For now they are the safety net on the
# highest-consequence code.

# Default: any change needs a review from the team.
*                                               @ianisharya @manu2raj

# The database layer and every migration. Schema changes are close to
# irreversible once they have run in production, so they get the highest care.
/apps/api/migrations/                           @ianisharya @manu2raj
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/db/                     @ianisharya @manu2raj

# Security: authentication, authorization, the single policy decision point.
# A mistake here is silent until it is exploited.
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/security/               @ianisharya @manu2raj

# Money and access. These modules decide who has paid and who may enter,
# and a subtle error is both expensive and hard to unwind.
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/modules/commerce/       @ianisharya @manu2raj
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/modules/payments/       @ianisharya @manu2raj
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/modules/entitlement/    @ianisharya @manu2raj

# Credentials. A forged or wrongly revoked certificate damages the thing
# the platform sells, its credibility.
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/modules/credential/     @ianisharya @manu2raj

# The AI gateway, guardrails, tutor memory, and tool authorization. This is
# where learner data and model authority meet, so it is reviewed closely.
/apps/api/src/neuvitech/modules/ai/             @ianisharya @manu2raj

# The pipeline and infrastructure. A change here affects every environment
# and every deploy.
/.github/                                       @ianisharya @manu2raj
/infrastructure/                                @ianisharya @manu2raj
/.devcontainer/                                 @ianisharya @manu2raj

# The documentation set is the source of truth. A change here changes how
# everyone understands and builds the system.
/docs/                                          @ianisharya @manu2raj

# The governance files themselves.
/CONTRIBUTING.md                                @ianisharya @manu2raj
/SECURITY.md                                    @ianisharya @manu2raj
/CODEOWNERS                                     @ianisharya @manu2raj
/LICENSE                                        @ianisharya @manu2raj
